/E (Yet this innovation exists alongside fragile institutions. Some governments tolerate limited political opposition, but others still restrict dissent, control the press, or shut down the internet during elections. While Kenya maintains a degree of openness, Ethiopia, Uganda, and Eritrea remain tightly controlled.)
