1493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (For countries like Comoros, Guinea-Bissau, and Mauritius, this was their first time cutting off access entirely, leaving millions without communication, banking, and essential online services. Most of these blackouts were triggered during protests or elections, as governments sought to control the flow of information and limit online mobilization.)
/E (For countries like Comoros, Guinea-Bissau, and Mauritius, this was their first time cutting off access entirely, leaving millions without communication, banking, and essential online services. Most of these blackouts were triggered during protests or elections, as governments sought to control the flow of information and limit online mobilization.)
/Pg 34 0 R
>>
endobj
1494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (Some cases stood out. In Kenya, Telegram was blocked during a nation-wide protest, while Uganda has continued its long-running Facebook ban, showing how digital restrictions can become deeply entrenched. )
