1515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Africa has the youngest population in the world, with about 60% under the age of 25. Yet, many young people feel shut out of the decisions shaping their countries. This frustration has increasingly spilled into the streets, driving powerful waves of youth-led protests across the continent. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [20 21]
>>
endobj
1516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (From demands for jobs and better governance to calls for justice and accountability, these movements reflect a generation unwilling to remain silent.)
/Pg 35 0 R
>>
endobj
1517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Social media has become a critical tool in this struggle, helping young Africans mobilize fast, coordinate leaderless actions, and amplify their voices globally. But governments have often responded with harsh crackdowns, using force, intimidation, and restrictive laws to silence dissent. This growing distrust in institutions has turned protest into a last resort for many.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
